<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 1.2 · Fishing & Thieving" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="1-2" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 1.2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Build movement stats, food, cash and the basic quest skill foundation.</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">This section converts the Wintertodt bank into useful account stats. Quest XP replaces manual melee training, Fishing supplies food, Barbarian Fishing supplies passive Agility/Strength, and Thieving supplies the cash reserve needed for the rune and Crafting purchases in 1.3.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="The important endpoints are actual 65 Fishing, actual 50 Agility, 60 Cooking, full Rogue equipment and at least 1.35m liquid GP. Thieving stops when the cash target is met, not at an arbitrary level. The route also completes the low-level quest foundation."
        stats={["Actual 65 Fishing", "Actual 50 Agility", "60 Cooking", "Actual 50 Thieving for Rogue's Den", "At least 1.35m liquid GP before leaving the section"]}
        unlocks={["Druidic Ritual / Herblore", "Sleeping Giants / Giant Foundry", "Tempoross fishing supplies; Angler outfit optional", "Waterfall Quest and Fight Arena combat XP", "Tree Gnome Village / spirit-tree access", "Full Rogue outfit", "Stored My Arm quest items"]}
      />

      <RouteStep id="i12-foundation" number="1" title="Clear the low-level quest foundation before the long Fishing grind">
        <p><strong>Use the live bank, not assumed Wintertodt drops:</strong> keep the reusable tools from 1.1 and withdraw only each quest's preparation below. Refill missing tools at Lumbridge General Store or the Varrock sawmill. Use available Reward Cart coins first; if a shop bill exceeds them, the <strong>East Ardougne silk-stealing/selling loop from 1.1</strong> supplies a repeatable early cash fallback. Do not count the later 1.35m cash stop as money already earned.</p>
        <p>Complete these quests one at a time:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Doric's Quest</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Goblin Diplomacy</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Witch's House</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Druidic Ritual</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Shield of Arrav</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Children of the Sun</strong> — this unlocks Varlamore and is required for several later Varlamore quests/activities.</li>
          <li><strong>Ethically Acquired Antiquities</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Sleeping Giants</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <ExpandableNote title="Eight foundation quests: ores, dyes, raw meat and unspun wool" label="Quest preparation">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Doric's Quest:</strong> <strong>6 clay, 4 copper ore and 2 iron ore, all unnoted</strong>. Check Wintertodt ore first. At the Rimmington mine, mine clay/copper and reach <strong>15 Mining</strong> with copper/tin if still below it, then mine the two iron ore. The Knight's Sword only required 10 Mining, so it does not guarantee that iron-mining gate. Bring your pickaxe; do not smelt Doric's ores.</li>
            <li><strong>Goblin Diplomacy:</strong> <strong>3 goblin mail, 1 orange dye and 1 blue dye</strong>. Search the crates around Goblin Village for the three mail. For dyes, give Aggie in Draynor <strong>3 redberries + 5 coins</strong> for red, <strong>2 onions + 5 coins</strong> for yellow, and <strong>2 woad leaves + 5 coins</strong> for blue; combine red and yellow into orange. Redberries grow south-east of Varrock, onions grow north of Rimmington, and offering Wyson in Falador Park <strong>20 coins</strong> gets two woad leaves. Dye only two mail, leaving one brown. If a crate/mail was missed, kill local goblins until the remaining mail drops.</li>
            <li><strong>Witch's House:</strong> bring <strong>2 cheese</strong> (one needed, one retry spare), <strong>leather gloves</strong>, food and a ranged/magic attack for the four experiments' safespots. Buy cheese at <strong>Wydin's Food Store in Port Sarim</strong> and leather gloves at <strong>Thessalia's clothes shop in Varrock</strong>; clue hunter gloves are not this item. An accessible magic starter is a <strong>staff of air from Zaff</strong> and <strong>500 mind runes from Aubury</strong> in Varrock, using Wind Strike on the standard spellbook; refill runes in small batches if needed. Remove metal armour that penalizes Magic accuracy. Steal fresh cakes in Ardougne for food rather than assuming Wintertodt left any. The house key, magnet and shed key are found during the quest.</li>
            <li><strong>Druidic Ritual:</strong> <strong>1 raw beef, 1 raw chicken, 1 raw rat meat and 1 raw bear meat</strong>. Kill one cow/chicken at the Lumbridge farms, one giant rat and one bear south-east of Varrock; the bear can be attacked with Magic from behind terrain. Keep all four meats <strong>raw</strong> and use the quest's cauldron to enchant them. This unlocks Herblore; reclaim the saved X Marks the Spot and Client of Kourend lamps from Veos and use them on it.</li>
            <li><strong>Shield of Arrav:</strong> choose a gang and arrange a partner in the <strong>opposite gang</strong> through the in-game <strong>OSRS SOA</strong> grouping/friends-chat resources. Phoenix members need <strong>20 coins</strong> and obtain Jonny the beard's report locally. Black Arm members need their partner's <strong>weapon-store key</strong> to obtain <strong>2 Phoenix crossbows</strong> from the Phoenix weapons store; normal shop crossbows do not substitute. For an Ironman handover, have the owner <strong>use the key or certificate half on the other player</strong>, then pick up the item placed at the recipient's feet. Exchange opposite certificate halves after the museum hand-in, combine them and give the finished certificate to King Roald. Bring the same refillable combat kit/food for the Weaponsmaster if fighting him. Stop only when the quest log says complete.</li>
            <li><strong>Children of the Sun:</strong> no outside items. Speak to Noah in Varrock Square and complete the local investigation. Afterwards, <strong>Regulus Cento outside Varrock's east gate</strong> provides the initial quetzal journey to Civitas illa Fortis; this is available without the later Twilight's Promise transport network.</li>
            <li><strong>Ethically Acquired Antiquities:</strong> no outside quest ingredients, but check <strong>25 Thieving</strong> and completed Shield of Arrav. Steal silk in Ardougne for a remaining level gap. The Fortis trader supplies the torn sail, Artima's crafting shop repairs it during the quest, and Betty supplies her notes. Return through Regulus's Varrock connection and walk to Port Sarim if saving the <strong>3,000-coin optional charter fare</strong>; do not assume a Fortis teleport spell is unlocked.</li>
            <li><strong>Sleeping Giants:</strong> <strong>3 oak logs, 1 unspun wool, 10 nails, a hammer and chisel</strong>. Chop the oak logs rather than relying on Wintertodt; shear one Lumbridge sheep and <strong>do not spin this wool</strong>. Use spare nails from Daddy's Home, or buy ten more at the Varrock sawmill. The Knight's Sword supplies the 15 Smithing gate. Take the tutorial metal from the foundry's supply crate. Pick up a bucket from the local pile, fill it at the waterfall and use it to handle the hot preform; ice gloves are optional.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Druidic Ritual</strong> is the important permanent unlock here because it opens Herblore. <strong>Sleeping Giants</strong> opens Giant Foundry for later Smithing. If Shield of Arrav requires another player/group, use the in-game grouping/partner resources and finish it before moving on rather than leaving one half of the certificate in the bank.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i12-runes" number="2" title="Buy the first exact rune stack in Port Sarim">
        <p>At <strong>Betty's Magic Emporium</strong>, bring your bank up to at least:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>1,500 mind runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>500 air runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1,500 water runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>500 earth runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>500 fire runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>200 body runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>100 chaos runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>150 death runes</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Count runes already bought for Witch's House; these are <strong>bank targets, not extra purchases</strong>. Keep <strong>6 air + 6 water + 6 earth runes</strong> separate for Waterfall Quest's hand-in. A staff does not replace those physical runes. The <strong>150 death runes</strong> are a later Desert Treasure reserve, not the normal early-quest ammunition; any spent runes must be replaced before that quest. Use restocks/other worlds for stock shortages and the established silk cash fallback for an actual coin deficit. The large nature/law/cosmic purchase for Mage Training Arena happens in 1.3.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i12-desert" number="3" title="Complete The Tourist Trap, then The Feud — and leave with the future dung already banked">
        <p><strong>Before the desert:</strong> read your actual levels: <strong>10 Fletching + 20 Smithing</strong> for Tourist Trap, then <strong>30 Thieving</strong> for The Feud. The Knight's Sword covers Smithing. If you skipped Wintertodt Fletching, cut ordinary logs into arrow shafts with a knife until 10; buy feathers from <strong>Gerrant in Port Sarim</strong> and add them to the shafts if you prefer. For a Thieving shortfall, use the established Ardougne stalls until 30. Neither the earlier quest names nor optional Wintertodt fletching guarantee those levels.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Desert clothing, retry materials and the quest's own equipment" label="Quest preparation">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>The Tourist Trap:</strong> bring <strong>a desert shirt, desert robe and desert boots, 3 bronze bars, 50 feathers and a hammer</strong>, plus your combat kit, food, filled waterskins and some coins. Buy desert clothing, filled waterskins, passes and bronze bars at <strong>Shantay's shop at Shantay Pass</strong>; buy the feathers from Gerrant. Take a spare shirt/robe if you want a ready replacement after the slave-clothing exchange. Crafting the prototype may fail: bank a few extra bronze bars and return to Shantay for more if needed rather than treating three as a guaranteed total. A knife can refill waterskins at desert cacti; a pickaxe covers the punishment-mining recovery if you are jailed. The slave outfit, key, plans, special pineapple and barrel come from quest NPCs/locations. Do not substitute an ordinary pineapple or barrel from the bank.</li>
            <li><strong>The Feud:</strong> bring <strong>at least 800 coins for the quest's local purchases</strong>, additional carpet/supply money, <strong>leather gloves</strong>, your refillable combat kit/food and the <strong>5 empty buckets</strong> below. Buy a <strong>Kharidian headpiece + fake beard</strong> from Ali Morrisane in Al Kharid and combine them into the disguise. Buy the quest's <strong>3 beers</strong> from Ali the Barman in Pollnivneach; the three banked for later are additional. Ali the Operator supplies the blackjack for the brief quest action, the snake charmer supplies the charm/basket after a coin donation, the kebab seller supplies the hot sauce and Ali the Hag makes the poison. You do not need a blackjacking training session or an already-banked poison. Refill ordinary gloves at Thessalia if lost. <strong>If the Tough Guy keeps despawning before you finish the fight</strong>, use the chaos runes bought in Step 2 for <strong>Wind Bolt at 17 Magic</strong> with your air staff; refill chaos runes at Betty/Aubury if needed. If still below 17, cast Wind Strike on low-level cows or goblins until the live level reaches it, then return. Return with the new spell and a replenished rune stack.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Bank between quests and desert trips.</strong> Take only the current quest's items plus food/water; use the bank chest at Shantay Pass to replace supplies. The Tourist Trap exchanges clothing and restricts equipment inside the mining camp, so equip the quest outfit when instructed. Use the quest safespots for the Mercenary Captain and Tough Guy; the foundation magic kit and the timed-fight recovery above provide the attack options.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Complete <strong>The Tourist Trap</strong> from start to finish and put <strong>both XP rewards into Agility</strong>. Then complete <strong>The Feud</strong>.</p>
        <p>For The Feud, buy <strong>5 loose empty buckets at Shantay Pass</strong> and bring them to the Ugthanki-dung section. Collect the <strong>brown Ugthanki dung</strong> produced after the hot sauce, not the differently coloured ordinary camel dung. You will use one bucket during the quest; finish the section with <strong>4 buckets of Ugthanki dung banked</strong>. These five buckets are separate from the 1,600-bucket Crafting allocation.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>3 buckets</strong> are reserved for <strong>My Arm's Big Adventure</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>1 bucket</strong> is a spare for the random-item portion of <strong>Forgettable Tale...</strong> if it asks for dung.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Also bank <strong>3 beers</strong> and <strong>3 vodkas</strong> while buying quest alcohol in Pollnivneach. These are explicit later-quest supplies.</p>
        <p>Before leaving the desert supply loop, stop at the <strong>Shantay Pass general store</strong> and buy/open <strong>16 Empty bucket packs</strong> for exactly <strong>1,600 empty buckets</strong>. The shop stocks 15 packs at a time, so buy 15, hop once, and buy the 16th. Bank the buckets noted. <strong>Do not use this stack for ordinary chores:</strong> 1.3 feeds all 1,600 to Drew at the Sandstorm grinder so the account can bank 1,600 buckets of sand for molten glass.</p>
        <div class="optional-efficiency"><strong>No blackjacking here.</strong> Once The Feud is complete, leave Pollnivneach. The dedicated Thieving block later in this subsection gives several methods.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i12-tempoross" number="4" title="Use Tempoross to build the Fishing bank">
        <p><strong>Entry gate:</strong> Tempoross requires <strong>actual 35 Fishing</strong>. Sea Slug in 1.1 awards useful early XP but does not reach 35 on its own. Read the skill tab and fly-fish trout/salmon at Barbarian Village or another comfortable spot until 35; bank at least the later <strong>10 trout and 15 salmon</strong> if you catch them here. Buy a <strong>fly fishing rod, harpoon and small fishing net</strong> and a starter <strong>1,000 feathers</strong> from Gerrant in Port Sarim, count any spare feathers first, and buy additional feather packs only if needed. Stop the bridge at 35.</p>
        <p><strong>First-timer loop:</strong> take Ferryman Sathwood south of Al Kharid bank to the Ruins of Unkah, then board Captain Dudi's boat on a Tempoross mass world. Bring your harpoon, small fishing net, rope, bucket and hammer; replace missing fishing tools at Gerrant and other tools at the established general stores. Spare rope, buckets and hammers are also available at the cove. Fish harpoonfish, optionally cook them, load the ammunition crates and fire the cannons; tether to a mast/pole for incoming waves or lightning. When Tempoross is subdued, fish its spirit pool for reward permits, then use a small net at the reward pool after the match. This is a Fishing skilling boss, not a normal combat boss. Leave at about 56 Fishing with a useful bank rather than chasing a unique drop.</p>
        <p>Train Fishing at <strong>Tempoross to about 56 Fishing</strong>. Standard mass worlds are fine. Prioritize a useful bank of fish, planks, gems and other supplies over squeezing every possible permit per hour.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Catherby charter-shop purchase:</strong> buy and bank <strong>1,600 soda ash</strong> and <strong>10 buckets of slime</strong>. The soda ash is the predictable Crafting/glass supply for 1.3; the slime is kept for later Prayer/quest utility.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i12-optional-angler" number="Optional" optional={true} title="Try Fishing Trawler for Angler only if you want a long-term Fishing investment">
        <p><strong>Full Angler is not a route gate.</strong> Its four pieces give a total <strong>2.5% Fishing-XP bonus</strong>, useful if you personally plan a very large later Fishing grind. This guide has no quest or skill checkpoint that needs the outfit, so skip the random set hunt by default.</p>
        <p>For a first visit, bring your <strong>axe and hammer</strong> (replace them at Khazard General Store if needed), then board <strong>Murphy's Fishing Trawler at Port Khazard</strong> on an official activity world. Chop attacking tentacles and repair the damaged railings until your contribution reaches at least <strong>50</strong>, then inspect the net west of the boat after each roughly six-minute round. Outfit pieces are random; do not plan an exact trip count. The one departure needed for Ardougne Easy was already handled in 1.1; this optional outfit hunt is a separate activity.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i12-quest-xp" number="5" title="Take the large combat-XP quests before manual combat training">
        <p>Complete these as separate quests:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Fight Arena</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Tree Gnome Village</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Waterfall Quest</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <ExpandableNote title="Logs, Waterfall runes, and the bank stop before Glarial's Tomb" label="Quest preparation">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Fight Arena:</strong> bring <strong>5 coins</strong> for the local bartender's Khali brew and your refillable magic/ranged kit with food. The Khazard helmet and armour are in a chest in the north-eastern house by the arena; the keys are obtained during the quest. Safespot the required fights using the arena obstacles. General Khazard's final fight is optional: leave after the required rescue rather than spending supplies on him.</li>
            <li><strong>Tree Gnome Village:</strong> bring <strong>6 ordinary logs</strong> for Commander Montai, plus the same combat kit/food. Chop six normal trees now if the bank is empty; oak logs do not replace them. The orbs are recovered in the quest, including from the Khazard warlord. Count remaining cast runes before leaving the bank, and buy only another small batch from Betty/Aubury if the preceding fights depleted them.</li>
            <li><strong>Waterfall Quest:</strong> bring <strong>1 rope and 6 each of air, water and earth runes</strong> for the waterfall stage. The rope is reusable; if the early stock is gone, buy one from Ned in Draynor or Aemad in Ardougne. Refill the eighteen physical runes from Betty/Aubury; an elemental staff is not accepted by the pillars. Golrie supplies <strong>Glarial's pebble</strong>, and Glarial's Tomb supplies her amulet/urn. <strong>Bank weapons, armour and all runes before entering that tomb</strong>; take the pebble, food and empty spaces. Make a second bank stop afterwards to retrieve the rope/runes for the waterfall dungeon. No mandatory fight or Prayer-potion supply is needed, but its high-level monsters can hurt you while moving.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Keep Glarial's pebble banked after Waterfall Quest</strong> for Roving Elves. If later lost, Golrie in the Tree Gnome Village dungeon can replace it. Replenish the food you actually use from Ardougne stalls or your Fishing bank; an optional teleport necklace is not required to walk these routes.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>These quests supply a large amount of early Attack/Strength XP. <strong>Do not start The Grand Tree yet</strong>; this guide saves it for 1.4 and completes it in one sitting.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i12-sidequests" number="6" title="Finish the self-contained travel/skill quests in this section">
        <p>Complete <strong>Fishing Contest</strong>, <strong>Observatory Quest</strong> and <strong>Dwarf Cannon</strong> as full quests. Before <strong>Death on the Isle</strong>, check <strong>actual 32 Agility and 34 Thieving</strong>; both are unboostable start gates. Earlier Thieving quest XP should cover 34, but the Tourist Trap Agility lamps alone do <em>not</em> guarantee 32. Train only the live Agility remainder with ordinary rooftop laps, then complete Death on the Isle (Children of the Sun is already done). Its two low-level foes are fought without equipment. This short Agility bridge counts toward the later actual-50 Rogue's Den checkpoint; it is not additional total Agility grinding. Keep the <strong>heavy fishing rod</strong> from Barbarian Training when you unlock Barbarian Fishing.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Contest bait, Observatory parts, and reaching Aldarin" label="Quest preparation">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Fishing Contest:</strong> <strong>5 coins, a normal fishing rod, a spade, 1 garlic and 1 red vine worm</strong>. Buy the normal rod from Gerrant (the fly fishing rod is different), or bring another 5 coins to buy one from Grandpa Jack in Hemenster. Take garlic from the cupboard upstairs in Morgan's house in Draynor. Squeeze through the loose northern fence into McGrubor's Wood, use the spade on a red vine to get the worm, and avoid its guard dogs. The dwarf at White Wolf Mountain gives the fishing pass; return there for a replacement. If a failed attempt used the worm, dig another. Sea Slug already covers 10 Fishing.</li>
            <li><strong>Observatory Quest:</strong> <strong>3 ordinary planks, 1 bronze bar and 1 molten glass</strong>. Use the three planks reserved from Daddy's Home; if spent, have the Varrock sawmill turn three normal logs into planks for 300 coins. Buy the bronze bar from Shantay, or smelt one copper + one tin ore at a furnace. At any furnace, make <strong>one molten glass from one of the seven early buckets of sand + one soda ash</strong>; if that stock is gone, buy the pair from a charter shop. Keep it molten for the professor instead of blowing it into an item. The goblin kitchen supplies the quest's lens mould. Bring food and collect a <strong>superantipoison dose from the spawn in the ruined building north of the Observatory</strong> before entering the dungeon; its spiders can poison. Collect another spawning dose if needed on a longer trip.</li>
            <li><strong>Dwarf Cannon:</strong> bring the <strong>hammer</strong> from your tools; one also spawns in the building east of Captain Lawgof. He supplies replacement railings and the repair toolkit, while Nulodion supplies the mould/notes later. <strong>Do not buy a dwarf multicannon or cannonballs</strong>: neither is required to finish this quest. Keep the ammo mould afterwards.</li>
            <li><strong>Death on the Isle:</strong> no outside quest items. After the live level checks, use <strong>Regulus's Varrock–Fortis quetzal</strong>, walk south-west across the Avium Savannah to <strong>Sunset Coast</strong>, and pay <strong>Antonia 20 coins</strong> for the boat to Aldarin. This works before fairy rings and Twilight's Promise. A charter ship to Aldarin is another paid option. Talk to <strong>Patzi at the entrance to Villa Lucens</strong>. Steal the butler uniform from the wardrobe in the house north of the villa; the other investigation objects are obtained during the quest. Bank any following kitten before entering. Bank combat gear for the quest's restricted fights as instructed, and use the local supplies.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <p><strong>Starting ordinary Barbarian Fishing:</strong> walk to <strong>Otto's Grotto beside the lake south-west of the Barbarian Outpost</strong>. Ask Otto about fishing, then search under his bed for the <strong>heavy fishing rod</strong>. It requires <strong>48 Fishing, 15 Agility and 15 Strength</strong> to start; the completed Tempoross, Tourist Trap and Waterfall blocks cover these, but read the live levels if returning to a partially completed route. Use <strong>feathers</strong> as bait: count those left from the earlier fly-fishing bridge, buy another small batch from Gerrant if needed, and refill only when running short. Fish the leaping-fish spots by Otto's lake with this rod; the ordinary fly fishing rod does not work there. Keep the heavy rod for later quests.</p>

      <TrainingOptions id="i12-fishing-agility-training" skill="Fishing / Agility" target="actual 65 Fishing + actual 50 Agility" why="65 Fishing lets an Ironman catch replacement raw karambwan after Tai Bwo Wannai Trio teaches the method, including if the quest's supplied fish burns; it is a useful supply breakpoint, not a universal Quest Cape gate. Barbarian Fishing also supplies passive Agility and Strength, but Fishing 74 has no mandatory consumer." recommended="Use the ordinary heavy-rod Barbarian Fishing loop to actual 65 Fishing: catch normally and drop fish when the inventory fills. Then read live Agility XP. If below 50, run ordinary rooftop laps for only the remainder and stop at actual 50. No 3-tick or cut-eat technique is assumed." relaxed="If you prefer fewer rooftop laps, keep ordinary Barbarian Fishing past 65 Fishing until Agility is actually 50. Your Fishing may naturally reach roughly 70–74 or higher; those extra levels are the consequence of your relaxed Agility choice, not a required Fishing target." resource="A knife can be used to let automatic gutting process leaping fish for small Cooking XP and bait recycling if you enjoy it. The default drops fish, so count no guaranteed Cooking XP or banked food from this block. Keep the separate 10 cooked trout and 15 cooked salmon quest reserve." fast="Ordinary rooftop Agility after Fishing 65 is the faster overall default. High-input tick manipulation is optional and never required." />

      <TrainingOptions id="i12-cooking-training" skill="Cooking" target="60" why="High-intensity Barbarian Fishing can generate substantial Cooking XP at the same time. Because this guide does not assume cut-eating, Cooking gets its own explicit checkpoint instead." recommended="Cook level-appropriate fish banked from Tempoross and early Fishing on a nearby range until actual 60 Cooking. Trout needs 15 Cooking and salmon needs 25. If the bank has no fish you can cook yet, kill Lumbridge cows and cook their raw beef until 15, then cook your trout before moving to salmon or higher-level fish." relaxed="Do the Cooking in several bankstanding/range sessions between quests. Cook and bank 10 trout and 15 salmon for the later quests, then cook the rest of your fish. Keep those finished fish out of your training-food withdrawals." resource="If the fish bank runs short, use your fly fishing rod and feathers at Barbarian Village for more trout/salmon, bank the catch and cook it. Refill feathers at Gerrant; stop gathering once cooking the usable fish meets the remaining XP and leaves 10 cooked trout plus 15 cooked salmon reserved." fast="Hosidius Mess Hall or other active methods can fill a short gap, but they are not required." />

      <RouteStep id="i12-rogues" number="7" title="Get the full Rogue outfit before the main Thieving grind">
        <p><strong>Bridge the real entry gate first:</strong> Rogue's Den and Wealthy Citizens both need <strong>actual 50 Thieving</strong>; Chapter 1.1 and The Feud do not guarantee it. Check your level. If below 25, steal from East Ardougne's bakery stall; from 25 to 50, use the Hosidius fruit stalls (the eastern pair near the beach avoids guard dogs) in ordinary batches. This is a short, more clicky bridge, not a new long-term blackjacking default. Your Agility checkpoint above supplies the Den's other actual-50 gate.</p>
        <p>Once your Agility and Thieving allow it, complete Rogue's Den until you have the <strong>full Rogue outfit</strong>. The double-pickpocket loot is a permanent account upgrade and makes later Ardougne Knights/Master Farmers more useful.</p>
        <p>For a first visit, enter the trapdoor in <strong>Burthorpe's Toad and Chicken inn</strong> and speak to Brian O'Richard. Bank all gear/inventory items; the maze supplies what it needs. Follow the trap/lock route to the safe, claim a rogue equipment crate, and repeat until all five pieces are owned. The outfit doubles pickpocket loot, including house keys from wealthy citizens; it does not multiply the value of the valuables stolen inside a house. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Rogues%27_Den" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Den map and trap guide</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Wealthy Citizens first-timer loop:</strong> with Children of the Sun complete and actual 50 Thieving, travel to the <strong>Civitas illa Fortis bazaar</strong> in Varlamore. When a street urchin distracts a wealthy citizen, click once to auto-pickpocket for a short window; repeat for house keys. Use a key on one of the marked wealthy houses, avoid the patrol inside, steal valuables, then sell them to <strong>Oriana beside the west Fortis bank</strong> for liquid coins. Bank useful jewellery separately. Rogue equipment doubles keys but is not required to operate the activity. Check liquid coins, not a projected Thieving level; stop when the cash target below is met.</div>

      <TrainingOptions id="i12-thieving-training" skill="Thieving / cash" target="at least 1.35m liquid GP" why="The liquid cash pays for the MTA rune stock, Crafting materials and travel infrastructure in 1.3. Actual 50 Thieving and full Rogue were secured immediately above; no higher Chapter 1 Thieving level is required." recommended="After full Rogue, use Wealthy Citizens and Stealing Valuables for relaxed money plus Thieving XP. Sell valuables for coins, check the actual liquid balance, and stop as soon as it reaches 1.35m. Record your live Thieving level; do not continue merely for 72 or 77." relaxed="If other income already put at least 1.35m liquid GP in the bank, no extra Wealthy Citizen session is needed. Ardougne Knights with Rogue are a familiar alternative if you still need coins, though check that the cash target—not just XP—is met." resource="Master Farmers are a seed-income choice, not a reliable substitute for the cash checkpoint. Reserve the 1.35m for the coming purchases; banked items are not yet liquid coins." fast="Blackjacking is an optional high-input XP method, not this route's default or a reason to overshoot the cash stop." />

      <RouteStep id="i12-finish" number="8" title="Leave 1.2 only after the cash, food and movement targets are actually met">
        <p>Before moving on, confirm:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Actual 50+ Thieving and the full Rogue outfit</strong>; record live Thieving XP, without assuming a higher level from the cash session</li>
          <li><strong>At least 1.35m liquid GP</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Actual 50+ Agility</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Actual 65+ Fishing</strong> (possibly higher if Barbarian Fishing supplied the relaxed Agility remainder)</li>
          <li><strong>60 Cooking</strong></li>
          <li><strong>10 cooked trout + 15 cooked salmon</strong> still banked</li>
          <li><strong>1,600 empty buckets</strong> reserved for the Sandstorm grinder</li>
          <li><strong>1,600 soda ash</strong> reserved for molten glass</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Keep your <strong>full Rogue outfit, 4 Ugthanki dung, beers/vodkas, 1,600 buckets, 1,600 soda ash and rune stack</strong> banked. If you chose the optional Trawler investment, keep any Angler pieces too; no later required step assumes them. 1.3 deliberately spends the mandatory preparation on permanent infrastructure.</p>
